<title>USA: DeCrane Aircraft cuts IPO price.</title>
<headline>DeCrane Aircraft cuts IPO price.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>DeCrane Aircraft Holdings Inc has cut the estimated price to buy shares in its initial public offering to $12 to $13.50 each, according to underwriter Schroder, Wertheim &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The price range had been $13 to $15. The proposed trading symbol on the Nasdaq is &quot;DAHX&quot;.</p>
<p>About 2.6 million shares will be offered in the IPO, which is due to price late Monday or Tuesday for trading during the next trading day. Of the total number of shares, 2.5 million wll be offered by the Copley, Ohio based company.</p>
<p>Decrane makes avionics components.</p>
</text>
